 To avoid missing important updates—such as referral questionnaires or interview scheduling links—please check your Personal Status Board regularly. For added convenience, you can also enable text (SMS) notifications. To do this, log in to your Personal Status Board and select “Update My Contact Information.” This posting may require completion of additional referral questions (RQs). You can access these RQs via an email that will be sent to you after the posting's closing date or by visiting your JobAps Personal Status Board (Certification Questionnaires section). Your responses to these RQs must be submitted by the questionnaire's expiration date. Please regularly check your email and JobAps Personal Status Board for notifications. Please check your SPAM and/or Junk folders on a daily basis in the event an email provider places auto-notification emails in a user's spam. Read through this helpful link to prepare for your interview. Although applicants will receive correspondence via email, as a backup they are also encouraged to sign on to their Personal Status Board on a daily basis to monitor their status, view all emailed notices and complete tasks required in the recruitment process. Note: At any point during the recruitment process, applicants may be required to submit additional documentation which support their qualification(s) for this position. These documents may include: a cover letter, resume, performance reviews, attendance records, supervisory references, licensure, etc., at the discretion of the hiring agency. Interviews will be limited to candidates whose experience and training most closely meet the requirements of the position. The immediate vacancy is listed above, however, applications to this recruitment may be used for future vacancies in this job class in the next twelve (12) months. Candidates who are offered and accept a position with the State of Connecticut are bound by the State Code of Ethics for Public Officials and State Employees which is available at www.ct.gov/ethics. Connect With Us: Due to the large volume of applications received, we are unable to provide confirmation of receipt or status during the recruitment process. Updates will be available through your JobAps portal account. Should you have any questions pertaining to this recruitment, please contact Francesca Poole, poole1@southernct.edu . Follow the State of Connecticut on LinkedIn. PURPOSE OF JOB CLASS (NATURE OF WORK) In a state agency this class is accountable for performing a full range of basic tasks in the cleaning and maintenance of buildings. EXAMPLES OF DUTIES Performs custodial tasks and maintenance of areas such as dormitories, classrooms, offices, auditoriums, wards, kitchens, dining rooms and lavatories including outdoor areas (i.e. trash around buildings); Dusts, mops, sweeps, scrubs, strips, waxes and polishes floors using appropriate equipment such as floor polishers and buffers; Washes, dusts and polishes glass including windows, woodwork, walls, furniture and metal equipment; Makes beds; Checks, marks, stores and issues linens, blankets, and clothing (limited to individual’s work area not to include counting and inspection for a larger area); Collects and counts soiled laundry; Distributes, empties and sterilizes glassware, wash basins and bedpans; Sweeps walks; Collects and disposes of trash; Reports needs for repairs; Performs minor maintenance; Runs errands; Inspects buildings for damage and reports conditions to supervisor; May change light bulbs and replace fuses; May lubricate or tighten door hinges, drawers, cabinets, etc.; May replace ceiling or floor tiles; May remove snow and ice from stairways and walkways around buildings; May sand and salt stairways and walkways; May move furniture and/or set-up classrooms; Performs related duties as required. KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITY Skills interpersonal skills; oral and written communication skills; Ability to follow oral and written instructions; operate, care for and perform minor maintenance on tools and equipment used in daily work; keep records. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Any experience and training which would provide the knowledge, skills and abilities listed above. SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS Incumbents in this class may be required  by the appointing authority to possess and retain  appropriate current licenses, permits, and/or certifications. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Incumbents in this class must have adequate physical strength, stamina, physical agility and visual and auditory acuity, and must maintain such physical fitness as to be able to perform the duties of the class. A physical examination may be required. WORKING CONDITIONS Incumbents in this class may be required to lift moderate to heavy weights and may be exposed to risk of injury from equipment and/or individuals. Conclusion AN AFFIRMATIVE ACTION/EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER The State of Connecticut is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer and strongly encourages the applications of women, minorities, and persons with disabilities. ACKNOWLEDGEMENT As defined by Sec. 5-196 of the Connecticut General Statutes, a job class is a position or group of positions that share general characteristics and are categorized under a single title for administrative purposes.  As such, a job class is not meant to be all-inclusive of every task and/or responsibility. Click on a link below to apply for this position: Fill out the\n        Supplemental Questionnaire and \n        Application NOW using the Internet. Apply Online E-mail Phone: (860) 713-5205 8am - 4:30pm M-F Powered by About CT Policies Accessibility Directories Social Media © 2026 CT.GOV Connecticut's Official State Website Please enable JavaScript to enhance your experience using this website. Many features of this site utilize JavaScript. Cookie Policy Our sites use cookies to enable functionality, analyze visitor traffic, and deliver a better user experience. By clicking 'Accept' below or continuing to use this website, you agree to accept cookies on this browser.  For more information, please review our Cookie Policy . Accept Dismiss"
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/part-time-lecturer-biology": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer",
      "description": "Part-time Lecturer - Biology | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings Part-time Lecturer - Biology Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact Part-time Lecturer - Biology The Biology department seeks to fill several part-time lecturer positions. Especially desired are individuals with experience and qualifications to teach general biology, botany, and anatomy & physiology. A Master's degree is required with a preference for biology. Applicants with Master's degrees in related fields will also be considered. To apply, submit a cover letter, résumé, one letter of reference that addresses quality of teaching, and copies of transcripts to the Biology department chairperson (electronic or hard copy). Dr. Rachel Jeffrey Biology Department 501 Crescent Street New Haven, CT 06515 jeffreyr1@southernct.edu 203-392-6211 Unofficial transcripts are acceptable. Review of applications will begin as received and continue until the positions are filled. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/part-time-lecturer-mathematics": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer",
      "description": "Part-time Lecturer - Mathematics (Multiple Positions) | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings Part-time Lecturer - Mathematics (Multiple Positions) Part-time Lecturer - Mathematics (Multiple Positions) (Multiple Openings) The math department seeks to fill several part-time lecturer positions. Especially desired are individuals with experience and qualifications to teach elementary statistics, mathematics for elementary education, or intermediate algebra in an emporium setting. For those seeking to teach intermediate algebra, familiarity with ALEKS preferred. A Master's degree is required with a preference for mathematics or statistics. Applicants with Master's degrees in related fields will also be considered, but only with a Bachelor's degree in mathematics. To apply, submit a cover letter, résumé, one letter of reference that addresses quality of teaching, and copies of transcripts to the math department chairperson (electronic or hard copy) Aaron Clark Mathematics Department 501 Crescent Street New Haven, CT 06515 math.chair@southernct.edu 203-392-5493 Unofficial transcripts are acceptable. Review of applications will begin 4/1 and continue until the positions are filled. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/part-time-lecturer-finance": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer",
      "description": "Part-time Lecturer - Finance | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings Part-time Lecturer - Finance Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact Part-time Lecturer - Finance Department: Finance and Real Estate Rank: Part-time Lecturer Specialization(s): Corporate Finance, Investments, Fixed Income, Risk Management & Banking and Fintech. Southern Connecticut State University (SCSU) is a diverse and student-centered university dedicated to academic excellence, access, and service for the public good. Southern provides a supportive and welcoming environment for all members of its community through a campus-wide commitment to social justice and inquiry. Founded as a teacher’s college in 1893, Southern has evolved over the past century into a comprehensive public university of approximately 9,000 students, with significant external research funding, and offering graduate and undergraduate programs in the liberal arts and professional disciplines. We seek to instill in all students the value of discovery with the liberal arts and sciences serving as a foundation for professional development and life-long learning. The University is located in New Haven, Connecticut, a city rich and vibrant with arts and culture, home to many universities, and with easy access to New York City and Boston. The Department of Finance and Real Estate at the AACSB Accredited School of Business (SCOB) invites applications for Adjunct Instructors to teach Corporate Finance in the Undergraduate Program, and other courses   -as mentioned above-   in the MS Financial Risk Management Program from Fall 2025. The SCOB is housed in a brand-new 60,000 Sq. Ft. SCOB building with a Financial Markets Lab and a Bloomberg Lab. A focus on sustainability, professional development of students and business community engagement are woven throughout its programs.  Current undergraduate enrollment in the SCOB is about 1000 students. It also has an MBA program, and two newly launched MS Programs; Business Data Analytics and Financial Risk Management. Brief Description of Duties/Responsibilities Teach up to two Undergraduate Corporate Finance courses per semester. Teach up to two Graduate courses per semester in the abovementioned Finance fields. Required Qualifications Masters Degree in Finance, or Economics, or a closely related field at the time of appointment. Ability to teach in traditional classroom format only. Candidates with a Degree or Degrees in Economics should demonstrate significant graduate coursework in the above areas. Preferred Qualifications Strong preference for candidates with an A.B.D., or a Ph.D., or appropriate professional experience in the above areas. Application Process Please submit all documents as a single pdf file: letter of interest indicating interest in courses, current curriculum vitae (incl. contact information of all references), and unofficial graduate transcripts to:  Dr. Sandip Dutta, Chair, Department of Finance and Real Estate at finsearch1@southernct.edu . For best consideration, all materials should be received by April 30th, 2025.  The positions will remain open until filled and is subject to budgetary approval. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/part-time-instructors-school-of-business": {
      "title": "Part-time Instructors -School of Business",
      "description": "Part-time Instructors -School of Business | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Close Navigation Search Search Slide In Main Menu About The university, administration, history Admissions Apply to Southern Academics Programs, academic departments Student Life Student resources, living on campus, support services Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings Part-time Instructors -School of Business Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact Part-time Instructors -School of Business Departments: Accounting, Business Information Systems, Economics, Finance and Real Estate, Management, and Marketing Rank: Part-Time Instructors Southern Connecticut State University (SCSU) is a diverse and student-centered university dedicated to academic excellence, access, and service for the public good. Southern provides a supportive and welcoming environment for all members of its community through a campus-wide commitment to social justice and inquiry. Founded as a teacher’s college in 1893, Southern has evolved over the past century into a comprehensive public university of approximately 9,000 students, with significant external research funding, and offering graduate and undergraduate programs in the liberal arts and professional disciplines. We seek to instill in all students the value of discovery with the liberal arts and sciences serving as a foundation for professional development and life-long learning. The University is located in New Haven, Connecticut, a city rich and vibrant with arts and culture,  home to many universities, and with easy access to New York City and Boston. The AACSB Accredited School of Business (SCOB) invites applications for Adjunct Instructors to teach across its multiple disciplines in both the undergraduate and graduate programs. The School offers a Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (multiple concentrations) as well as a newly launched Bachelor of Science in Energy And Utility Leadership.  Graduate Programs include our STEM  Master of Business Administration, as well as two STEM Master of Science programs in Business Analytics and Financial Risk Management. The School also offers a Doctorate in Business Administration with an emphasis on resiliency studies. The SCOB is housed in a brand-new 60,000 Sq. Ft. building with a Financial Markets Lab and a Bloomberg Lab. A focus on sustainability, professional development of students and business community engagement are woven throughout its programs. Opportunity/Brief Description of Responsibilities Opportunity to teach up to two undergraduate and or graduate courses per fall and spring semester. Potential for winter intersession or summer teaching. Alternatives available to teach in either in traditional classroom format or using alternative delivery systems. Adjuncts may join the School’s Adjunct Faculty Council, where they may have a voice in leadership of the School and also discuss strengthening the adjunct faculty community. This reflects the School’s initiative to acknowledge the fine work of our adjunct community and provide support for their teaching, scholarship and service. Required Qualifications Masters Degree in the area of teaching. Preferred Qualifications A.B.D., Ph.D., D.B.A. or longitudinal professional experience in the area of teaching. Application Process Please submit all documents as a single zipped or pdf file: Letter of interest (include your discipline/area for preferred teaching assignment); Current curriculum vitae (include contact information of all references), and Unofficial graduate transcripts to: Dr. Prabhakar Gantasala, Associate Dean, School of Business at businesssearch1@southernct.edu . This is a rolling search; hence all positions will remain open as long as this ad is posted. All hiring is subject to budgetary approval. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-institutional-advancement-26": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant - Institutional Advancement | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant - Institutional Advancement Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Assistant - Institutional Advancement This is a temporary, part-time position, which may be renewed at the discretion of the University. Hours/Week: 19 hours per week.  The UA is expected to work 19 hours per week.  The exact schedule will be established between the Supervisor and the successful applicant to meet the needs of the department. Southern Connecticut State University is a diverse and student-centered university dedicated to academic excellence, access, and service for the public good. Southern provides a supportive and welcoming environment for all members of its community through a campus wide commitment to social justice. Founded as a teachers college in 1893, Southern has evolved over the past century into a comprehensive public university of more than 10,000 students, offering graduate and undergraduate programs in the liberal arts and professional disciplines. It is one of four universities in the Connecticut State Colleges and Universities System. The University is located in New Haven, a city rich with arts and culture, and less than 90 miles from New York City and 140 miles from Boston. Position Justification: Advancement Services supports and enhances the friend-raising and fundraising efforts of the University.  The Advancement Services Department needs a University assistant to help with inputting records and maintain data in our Raiser's Edge development database.  Works independently with minimal supervision. Specific Duties: Input current contact information for new constituents & update current data such as address, telephone, email changes. Code all outgoing solicitations with appeal codes. Enter donations into Raisers Edge (database) into appropriate constituent records – analysis of each donor record to ensure duplicate records are not created. Assist with organization of gifts for specific appeals.  This requires extensive knowledge of excel, multiple excel files, advanced Raisers edge database experience required. Assist with the build and maintenance of excel templates and spreadsheets for imports into database (must be able to use additional software tools such as import-o-matic). Process and assist with coordination of event registrations in Raisers edge Assist with general database maintenance.  When asked by supervisor, the duties would include: Tracking of returned mail (multi step process within excel and Raisers edge database). Remove duplicate constituents. Update student attributes such as athletics, clubs, positions held and other activities in order to solicit alumni in specific areas of interest.  This involves using multiple queries in database. Remove non-donor parent and student records. Assist with E-invitations to events and newsletters mailed. Provides assistance/training to other University Assistants as required. Other duties as needed. Preferred Qualifications, Experience, Requirements: B.S./B.A. degree preferred. Successful candidate must be responsible, detail oriented and well organized. Strong computer skills and ability to handle strictly confidential information. Preferred Qualifications, Experience, Requirements: Depending on experience and credentials, the hourly wage range is. Qualified applicants should send a cover letter, résumé, and list of three references to vernerm1@southernct.edu .  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Expected start date is as soon as possible. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-slh-26": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant – Department of Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant – Department of Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Assistant – Department of Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences Position: University Assistant Department: Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences Category: Part-time (max of 19hrs per week); 1-year appointment Date Posted: 08/06/2026 Application Deadline: Until Filled Department Description The Department of Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences offers a Bachelor of Science degree in Communication Disorders and a Master of Science degree in Speech-Language Pathology. The Department educates between 175 and 215 undergraduate students and clinically trains approximately 45 full-time graduate students per year. Undergraduate students are responsible for obtaining clinical observation hours, many of which are obtained in our on-site clinic. Each of the 45 graduate students rotates through a six-semester academic and clinical program. The on-site clinic serves approximately 120 clients in New Haven and surrounding communities with critical diagnostic and therapeutic intervention care related to developmental and acquired communication disorders. The Clinic Services program consists of the Southern Connecticut Audiology program, Center for Communication Disorders, and Access Network. Position Summary The billing and scheduling assistant will, under the direction of the Director of Clinical Education,  assist in guiding the graduate student workers, billing, record keeping, managing calendars, and providing administrative and coordination support to the Clinic faculty. The position will be paid with the clinic funds. Position Description Billing Manage memos, letters, faxes, and forms Assist on maintaining student and client records electronically Maintain client contact lists and monitor relevant Teams pages Answer phone calls relating to clinic operations Assist in compiling billing reports Work with graduate assistants to generate invoices and manage accounts payable Work with graduate assistants to manage scheduling of appointments Assist in maintaining inventory of clinic protocols Assist clinical instructors with paperwork Qualification 1-2 years’ experience as an administrative assistant Excellent computer skills (Excel, Word, etc.) Excellent time management skills and ability to multitask Strong organizational skills Associate or bachelor’s degree Strong verbal and written communication skills Application Instructions Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, current resume, and availability via email to Sujini Ramachandar ramachandas1@southernct.edu . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-fiscal-affairs-26": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant - Fiscal Affairs (Contracts and Procurement) | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant - Fiscal Affairs (Contracts and Procurement) Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Assistant - Fiscal Affairs (Contracts and Procurement) This is a temporary, part-time position, which may be renewed at the discretion of the University. Hours/Week:  19 hours per week.  The UA is expected to work 19 hours per week.  The exact schedule will be established between the Supervisor and the successful applicant to meet the needs of the department. Southern Connecticut State University is a diverse and student-centered university dedicated to academic excellence, access, and service for the public good. Southern provides a supportive and welcoming environment for all members of its community through a campus wide commitment to social justice. Position Summary The Part-Time Contract Support Assistant provides administrative support to the University’s Fiscal Affairs team by assisting with basic contract review, vendor documentation, and standardized agreements. Working up to 19 hours per week, this role focuses on routine contract tasks and helps ensure vendor paperwork aligns with established university, system, and state guidelines. Specific Duties Contract Review Support Assist in reviewing vendor purchase orders and agreements for standard terms and conditions. Flag common contractual provisions that are not permitted for state agencies using established guidance (e.g., indemnification, governing law). Prepare draft responses or standard language for vendor communications, subject to team review. Template-Based Agreements Prepare and process simple, templated agreements using pre-approved university forms. Ensure required fields and standard clauses are completed accurately and consistently. Route agreements for internal review and signatures as needed. Vendor Documentation Assistance Help maintain records of contracts, agreements, and related procurement documentation. Coordinate routine follow-ups with vendors regarding missing or corrected paperwork. Support basic communication with vendors using standard messaging. Research Support Assist in identifying existing state or cooperative contracts under direction. Gather information to support procurement staff in determining appropriate contract sources. Administrative Support Maintain organized electronic files and tracking logs. Provide general clerical support to the Business Services team as needed. Qualifications Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in a related field, or equivalent experience. Prior experience in an administrative, legal support, or clerical role preferred. Familiarity with basic contract terminology or legal documents (paralegal experience is a plus). Strong attention to detail and ability to follow established procedures. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Please send your resume to Nina Cote for consideration for this position. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-accounts-payable-26": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant – Accounts Payable | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant – Accounts Payable Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Assistant – Accounts Payable Position: University Assistant Department: Accounts Payable Category: Part-time Date Posted: 4.1.2026 Application Deadline: Until Filled Department Description The Accounts Payable Office supports the financial operations of the University by ensuring timely, accurate, and compliant processing of vendor payments. The department works closely with campus departments and external vendors to maintain financial integrity, provide excellent customer service, and uphold university and regulatory standards. Position Summary The University Assistant (UA) works under the supervision of the Accounts Payable Coordinator and assists with the daily operations of the Accounts Payable office. This position supports invoice processing, payment distribution, vendor maintenance, and compliance-related activities to ensure efficient and accurate financial operations. Position Description Process invoices for payment in accordance with university policies and procedures. Issue vendor payments via check, ACH, and other approved payment methods. Initiate and manage stop payment requests, coordinate reissuance of payments as necessary. Research and respond to vendor and departmental inquiries regarding payment status and discrepancies. Assist with the setup and maintenance of vendor records, including ACH/direct deposit enrollment and updates. Maintain accurate financial records within Banner and related systems. Research outstanding checks and prepare due diligence letters; track responses and returned mail. Support the escheatment process by preparing required documentation and ensuring compliance with state deadlines. Investigate and resolve bank discrepancies and payment-related issues. Assist with new vendor setup and updates to existing vendor information. Support the annual 1099 reporting process, including data review, correction, and preparation of forms to meet the January 31 deadline. Provide customer service support to campus departments and external vendors regarding payment inquiries. Assist with special projects and perform other duties as assigned by the Accounts Payable Coordinator. Qualification Experience in a financial, accounting, or administrative setting preferred. Strong organizational and multitasking abilities. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Familiarity with financial systems (e.g., Banner) is a plus. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. High level of professionalism and confidentiality. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Performs other duties and responsibilities related to those described above as needed. Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree preferred (or currently pursuing). Application Instructions Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, current resume, and availability via email to:  Dale Bodyk, Accounts Payable Coordinator, BodykD1@southernct.edu .  Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-alumni-donor-engagement-26": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant – Institutional Advancement (Alumni & Donor Engagement) | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant – Institutional Advancement (Alumni & Donor Engagement) Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Assistant – Institutional Advancement (Alumni & Donor Engagement) Position Title : University Assistant - Alumni & Donor Engagement Department : Alumni & Donor Engagement Division : Institutional Advancement Supervisor's Title : Associate Vice President for Alumni & Donor Engagement This is a temporary, part-time position, which may be renewed at the discretion of the University. Hours/Week: 19 hours per week.  The UA is expected to work 19 hours per week.  The exact schedule will be established between the Supervisor and the successful applicant to meet the needs of the department. Southern Connecticut State University is a diverse and student-centered university dedicated to academic excellence, access, and service for the public good. Southern provides a supportive and welcoming environment for all members of its community through a campus-wide commitment to social justice. Position Overview The University Assistant provides part-time administrative and programmatic support to the Offices of Alumni Relations, Donor Relations, and Annual Giving within Institutional Advancement. Working under the direction of the Associate Vice President for Alumni & Donor Engagement and designated professional staff, the University Assistant assists with day-to-day activities that support alumni engagement initiatives, donor communications, and advancement-related projects. The position contributes to the coordination of engagement efforts that foster meaningful connections between the University and its alumni, donors, students, and campus partners. Position Responsibilities Assists with administrative and operational support for alumni relations, donor relations, and annual giving initiatives. Provides limited support for digital and web-based communications, including assisting with content updates and distribution using platforms such as MyEmma, ThankView, Hustle, and the University website, under staff direction. Assists with basic data-related tasks within systems such as Raiser's Edge NXT and other advancement platforms, including data entry, list preparation, and running pre-defined reports, as directed by professional staff. Provides support for Institutional Advancement events, including assisting with event preparation, materials, registration processes, and day-of logistics. Assists with drafting and editing routine communications such as emails, invitations, and short announcements for alumni and donor audiences, subject to review by professional staff. Assists professional staff with coordinating assigned student workers by helping distribute tasks and monitoring completion of routine assignments. May assist professional staff with coordinating the work of student workers as assigned. Performs other related duties as assigned that support the overall goals of Alumni & Donor Engagement. Minimum Qualifications Required Demonstrated knowledge and ability in the use of personal computer equipment and standard office software such as Microsoft Office Suite. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in writing. Application Process Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, current resume and availability via email to Brett Santo at santob1@southernct.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Expected start date is as soon as possible. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-facilities-operations": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant - Department of Facilities Operations | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant - Department of Facilities Operations University Assistant - Department of Facilities Operations Department: Department of Facilities Operations Supervisor’s Title: Director of Architectural Services Position Summary The University Assistant (UA) will assist the Director and Assistant Director of Architectural Services, as an Architectural Assistant, with the daily operations within the Department of Facilities Operations. Specific Duties / Responsibilities Perform duties to assist as a CAD Specialist Assist with the Architectural needs in the design and administering of Minor Capital Projects. Assist with preparation of Minor Capital projects, including measuring of spaces and visual review of project spaces when needed. Assist with planning, programming, and design of Interior Spaces for DCS Administered Projects when needed. Assist with the planning and design of Fixture, Furniture and Equipment (FFE) components of Agency and DCS administered projects. Assist in the procurement of Fixture, Furniture and Equipment (FFE) components of Agency and DCS administered projects and assist in overseeing installation phase of the work. Position Qualifications / Requirements CAD software experience in AutoCAD and REVIT Architectural design and layout experience New and Renovation Design experience Fixture, Furniture and Equipment (FFE) selection and procurement experience Application Applicants should submit a letter of interest, resume, and three references to: Peter Visentin Director of Architectural Services Department of Facilities Operations Visentinp1@southernct.edu All application materials must be electronically submitted. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The work schedule would consist of a maximum of 19 hours per work week. Hourly salary dependent upon qualifications and will fall within the parameters of the current UA Hire Wage Guidelines scale chart. The expected start date is as soon as possible. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/employment-student-workers": {
      "title": "Employment - Student Workers",
      "description": "Employment - Student Workers | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Close Navigation Search Search Slide In Main Menu About The university, administration, history Admissions Apply to Southern Academics Programs, academic departments Student Life Student resources, living on campus, support services Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings Employment - Student Workers Employment - Student Workers To view student worker postings please visit the Center for Career Services website at careers.southernct.edu . SCSU is an Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity employer.  The University seeks to enhance the diversity of its faculty and staff.  People of color, women and persons with disabilities are strongly encouraged to apply. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/owll-trainer": {
      "title": "Office of Workforce and Lifelong Learning (OWLL) Trainer",
      "description": "Office of Workforce and Lifelong Learning (OWLL) Trainer | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Close Navigation Search Search Slide In Main Menu About The university, administration, history Admissions Apply to Southern Academics Programs, academic departments Student Life Student resources, living on campus, support services Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings Office of Workforce and Lifelong Learning (OWLL) Trainer Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact Office of Workforce and Lifelong Learning (OWLL) Trainer To be considered as a noncredit trainer in the University’s Office of Workforce and Lifelong Learning, please visit the OWLL Forms and Resources page . Please note that these are contract positions, and participants will not be employees of the University. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    },
    "https://inside.southernct.edu/human-resources/jobs/ua-cscu-qnt": {
      "title": "University Assistant",
      "description": "University Assistant – CSCU QNT | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Human Resources Home Human Resources Job Openings University Assistant – CSCU QNT Menu Home Job Openings Employee Benefits Forms Faculty Resource Guide Policies & Procedures Labor Relations - Contracts Faculty Senate Evaluation Documents » For Part-Time Faculty For Supervisors Hiring Students Student Employment Hiring Process Events Contact University Assistant – CSCU QNT Department: CSCU QNT Hours: 19 hours/week Reports to: Director of Center for QNT Position Summary The University Assistant provides logistical and administrative support for the Werth Industry Academic Fellowship (IAF) program and day-to-day student coordination functions at the Center for Quantum and Nanotechnology (QNT). The UA works closely with the DRI Administrative Assistant, Center Technician and Faculty Coordinator, and is overseen by the Center Director. The UA role ensures that IAF students are organized, informed, and supported throughout the fellowship period and beyond. Key Responsibilities Werth Industry Academic Fellowship (IAF) — Primary Responsibility Serve as the primary logistical point of contact for the Werth IAF program during the summer fellowship period and into the academic year. Ensure all fellows have completed and submitted required paperwork prior to program start, including onboarding forms, waivers, and agreements. This includes HR paperwork and timecards. Create and maintain Microsoft Teams folders and channels to organize summer IAF work, communications, and document storage. Coordinate and schedule student outings, site visits, and program events throughout the summer. Monitor student attendance and follow up when scheduled hours or commitments are not met. Outreach, Documentation & Events Assist with creating and publishing content to Center website and social media platforms (Instagram, LinkedIn, etc.) as needed. Assist in preparing outreach materials for prospective industry partners, academic collaborators, and new users. Qualifications Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook) and Microsoft Teams. Ability to manage multiple concurrent responsibilities and prioritize effectively. Ability to work independently and follow through on assigned tasks with minimal supervision. SCSU is an Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University seeks to enhance the diversity of its faculty and staff. People of color, women, veterans, and persons with disabilities are strongly encouraged to apply. To Apply Submit your resume and cover letter to cscu-nano@southernct.edu with “QNT University Assistant Opening” in the subject heading. Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
    }
  },
